; renameworld.eval — makes the scratch world the rename checks run in (W11).
; WorldTest removes it afterwards.
;
; The `reset` is only so the script ENDS IN PLAY: a run that stops on the title
; is a FAIL by the runner's rule, and WorldTest now reads every script's verdict
; (code-review C442) - a setup script that always failed would teach it to be
; skimmed. `state` after it, because a cold `reset` only STARTS the load: the
; next line is what waits for it, and without one the run ends mid-load.
logecho on
worlds new wt_ren
reset
state
